concepts.content:
From the image gradient, we can extract the edge strength $e(x,y)$, which is defined as the gradient magnitude:

$$\begin{aligned}
    e(x,y) &= \lVert \nabla \ell(x,y) \rVert   & \quad\quad \triangleleft \quad \texttt{edge strength}
\end{aligned}$$ 

The edge strength quantifies the intensity of the variation at pixel $(x,y)$.

