concepts.content:
From the image gradient, we can extract the edge orientation $\theta(x,y)$:

$$\begin{aligned}
    \theta(x,y) &= \angle \nabla \ell =  \arctan \left( \frac{\partial \ell / \partial y}{\partial \ell / \partial x} \right) & \quad\quad \triangleleft \quad \texttt{edge orientation}
\end{aligned}$$ 

The edge orientation is perpendicular to the gradient direction.

